<title>USA: Richmond Fed-March manufacturing, services indexes.</title>
<headline>Richmond Fed-March manufacturing, services indexes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond indexes monitoring manufacturing and service-sector activity.</p>
<p> MANUFACTURING SURVEY    April   March</p>
<p>  Shipments		    15     29</p>
<p>  New Orders		   25     25</p>
<p>  Backlog Orders	     10	2</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	 1     -2</p>
<p>  Average Workweek	    7     -1</p>
<p>  Prices Received	  0.37  -0.34</p>
<p>  Prices Paid		0.49   0.03</p>
<p> SERVICES SURVEY	   April   March</p>
<p>  Service Revenues	   33     43</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	11	9</p>
<p>  Service Wage		 16     23</p>
<p>  Retail Revenues	    36     57</p>
<p>  Retail Employees	    7	7</p>
<p>  Retail Wage		  23     41</p>
<p>  Shopper Traffic	    35     28</p>
<p>Note -- Each index equals the percentage of responding firms reporting increases minus the percentage reporting decreases. Prices received and prices paid are in response to the question &quot;What do you believe was the percentage price change in your industry on an annualized basis?&quot;</p>
<p>Results of the April manufacturing survey are based on responses from 93 of 179 firms queried. Results of the April service-sector survey are based on responses from 92 of 123 firms.</p>
</text>
